  "result": "Perfect! All 50 tests pass. I've added `addLine` and `removeLine` functions with comprehensive test coverage:\n\n**Added to `src/invoices.js`:**\n\n1. **`addLine(invoice, { sku, qty })`** \u2014 Returns `ok(newInvoice)`\n   - Validates invoice.status is 'draft' (NOT_DRAFT error)\n   - Validates qty as positive integer (QTY_INVALID error)\n   - Validates SKU exists (UNKNOWN_SKU error)\n   - If SKU already on invoice: increases that line's qty\n   - If SKU not on invoice: appends new line with product details\n   - Never mutates original invoice or its lines\n\n2. **`removeLine(invoice, sku)`** \u2014 Returns `ok(newInvoice)` or error\n   - Validates invoice.status is 'draft' (NOT_DRAFT error)\n   - Returns LINE_NOT_FOUND if SKU not on invoice\n   - Returns NO_LINES if it's the only line\n   - Creates new invoice without that line\n   - Never mutates original invoice or its lines\n\n**Added error codes:**\n- `NOT_DRAFT` \u2014 Can only edit invoices with status draft\n- `LINE_NOT_FOUND` \u2014 No line with that SKU on the invoice\n\n**Added 14 tests covering:**\n- Adding new lines and increasing existing quantities\n- Validation matching createInvoice\n- Rejection of non-draft invoices\n- Removing lines and error cases\n- Immutability and new object creation\n- Chaining multiple operations\n\nAll 50 tests pass (36 original + 14 new).",
